<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">A Famosa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1511</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Porta de Santiago</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A Famosa was the fortress built by the Portuguese under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-de-albuquerque">Afonso de Albuquerque</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> after they captured the city in 1511. It enclosed the hill and town by the river and withstood many sieges until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> took it in 1641. The British demolished most of it in the early 19th century, and only the gate called the Porta de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> survives.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/a-famosa.jpg" alt="A Famosa" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chongkian · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_Famosa_Fortress.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
